==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|sól|lang=non}} from {{proto|Germanic|sunnon|lang=is}} from {{proto|Indo-European|sóh₂wl̥|lang=is}}. Cognate with Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrl|слъньцє|tr=slŭnĭce|lang=cu}}, Latin {{term|sol|sōl|lang=la}}, Ancient Greek {{term|ἥλιος|sc=polytonic|tr=hēlios|lang=grc}}, Sanskrit {{term|sc=Deva|सूर|tr=sūra|lang=sa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/souːl/|lang=is}} ({{audio|Sól.ogg|listen}})
*: {{rhymes|ouːl|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|sólar|sólir}}

# the [[sun]] {{gloss|star around which the Earth revolves}}
#: '''''Sólin''' er [[björt]].''
#:: The '''sun''' is [[bright]].
# [[sun]] {{gloss|applied to any star or used metaphorically}}

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-f-s2|s|ó|l}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|the sun}} {{l|is|sunna}} (''poetic'')

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|sólarljós}}
* {{l|is|sólmyrkvi}}
* {{l|is|forsæla}}

[[Category:is:Astronomy]]
[[Category:is:Weather]]

